-The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same directory is published a second time in a machine-readable form, carrying the same veterinarians and the same specialties for a program to read `[REQ-VET-003]` (stated 2026-08-15).
+
+Either form of the directory can be asked for one specialty, and then lists only the veterinarians holding it. The specialty is named in full and letter case does not matter; naming part of a specialty matches nobody. Naming a specialty no veterinarian holds is a valid request answered with an empty list rather than a failure. Naming nothing, or nothing but spaces, lists the whole directory as before. Paging through a narrowed directory keeps the narrowing `[REQ-VET-004]` (stated 2026-08-15). Neither form offers a control for choosing a specialty; the narrowing is asked for in the request itself.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the machine-readable directory is requested, then it carries every veterinarian with the specialties each holds.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty that at least one veterinarian holds, when either form of the directory is asked for it, then only those veterinarians are listed.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given that same specialty named in another letter case, when the directory is asked for it, then the same veterinarians are listed.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when the directory is asked for it, then the request succeeds and the list is empty.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given no specialty in the request, when either form of the directory is opened, then every veterinarian is listed as before.
+- `[REQ-VET-004]` given a narrowed directory spanning more than one page, when a further page is opened, then the narrowing still applies.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. A specialty named only in part matches no veterinarian, even when a whole specialty starts with those letters.
+3. A specialty that is empty or nothing but spaces is treated as though none were named, as an empty owner search is.
+4. The machine-readable form lists every matching veterinarian at once; it is not paged.
 
